% composition-bridge: Listen for how a contemporary country-pop track combines a direct story, a firm backbeat, short hooks and contrasting vocal articulation.
% composition-context: Shania Twain is an Ontario-born Canadian singer-songwriter whose work connects country writing with pop production and performance.
% composition-distance: Original three-note E-G-A classroom tune and lyric; no hook, words, chord sequence, guitar figure or drum pattern from "Faded Blue Jeans" is used.
% improv: {"id":"A","bars":"3-4","role":"solo caller","prompt":"Choose how the boots answer","choices":["two accented stomps","four light taps","one silent pose"],"replyBars":2}
% improv: {"id":"B","bars":"7-8","role":"class","prompt":"Choose the last articulation","choices":["smooth","detached","accent then smooth"],"replyBars":2}
% dossier-function: original Grade 1 country-pop listening bridge; a caller sings the first two bars, the class answers, and a student selects an accented, detached or smooth body-percussion reply
% dossier-elements: eight bars in 2/4; E-G-A only (mi-so-la in C), E4-A4 range; quarters, paired eighths and quarter rests; accent, legato and staccato options; call-and-response form 2+2+2+2
% dossier-practice: Rehearsal key C; written range E4-A4. Quarter note = 92 target, begin at 76. Echo the spoken rhythm, sing on solfa, add words, then add optional seated foot taps or hand pats. Keep stomping low-force and optional.
% dossier-accompaniment: Newly authored C-F-G country-pop classroom pattern: bass root on beat 1 and light clap or brush on beat 2. Optional open-string ukulele or guitar may play one chord per bar; no imitation of Twain's arrangement.
% dossier-lyrics: Original English lyric about following a bright path. "Boots" may become shoes, wheels, hands or any learner-chosen travel word without changing the learning target.
% dossier-honesty: AI-assisted original composition for Grand Central Stationery, 11 November 2026; not traditional, not by Shania Twain and not an arrangement or soundalike.
% dossier-licence: CC0 1.0 for melody, lyric, harmony and ABC; the reference song and recording remain copyrighted.
% dossier-respect: Present Twain as a working Canadian songwriter and producer-crossing artist, not as a costume or a generic symbol of rural life. Country music contains many communities and approaches.
% dossier-review: Grade 1 music teacher, accessibility reviewer, second score reader and student singing trial; all reviews still required
